# Generated cloud sink/source connector configs carry an injected connection.password.
# The clinic side already ignores its generated/ dir; the cloud side never got the
# equivalent, so `git add -A` here would commit live credentials to a PUBLIC remote.
# (sync-core F-010, second trap.)
debezium/cloud/connectors/*.json
debezium/cloud/connectors/generated/

# --- cloud node, 2026-09-02 ---
# The live override carries three literal passwords (POSTGRES_PASSWORD,
# OPENELIS_DB_PASSWORD, OPENMRS_ATOMFEED_PASSWORD) and this remote is PUBLIC.
# The committed .example beside it enumerates every key with ${VAR} placeholders.
# Hand-rolled version control from before this repo was used properly.
*.bak-*
# 10 MB OpenELIS seed dump (carries credential hashes) and 54 MB of built
# front-end assets -- neither belongs in git; both are reproducible.
debezium/cloud/openelis-starter.sql
debezium/cloud/htdocs/
